; RUN: circt-yosys | FileCheck %s
; RUN: circt-yosys --help | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HELP
; REQUIRES: yosys

; Yosys' own log goes to stderr, so stdout carries only the tool's output and
; needs no filtering here.

; The CIRCT half: a hardcoded hw.module, parsed and printed back.
; CHECK:      input hw.module:
; CHECK-NEXT: hw.module @demo(in %a : i8, in %b : i8, in %c : i8, out y : i8)
; CHECK-NEXT:   comb.and %a, %b : i8
; CHECK-NEXT:   comb.or %0, %c : i8
; CHECK-NEXT:   hw.output

; The Yosys half: one RTLIL cell per Comb operation, built through the Yosys API
; in the same translation unit.
; CHECK: built \demo with 2 cells

; Every pass in the pipeline runs. `techmap` reads a technology library out of
; Yosys' data directory and `abc` execs the `yosys-abc` binary, so reaching the
; end of this list also proves both runtime paths resolved -- which for a binary
; in `bin/` means the executable-relative lookup, not the compiled-in fallback.
; CHECK: running: hierarchy -check -top demo
; CHECK: running: techmap
; CHECK: running: abc -g AND,OR,XOR
; CHECK: running: opt_clean

; `abc -g AND,OR,XOR` maps the design onto exactly those gates, and an 8-bit
; `(a & b) | c` needs one of each per bit.
; CHECK:      cells in \demo:
; CHECK-DAG:    8x $_AND_
; CHECK-DAG:    8x $_OR_

; HELP: circt-yosys - drive Yosys as a library from CIRCT
